# Cloudflare Pages — https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects/
#
# Every public route (/, /blog, /blog/:slug) is its own real prerendered
# static file (see scripts/prerender.mjs) — no SPA fallback needed there, so
# a nonexistent URL correctly 404s (see public/404.html) instead of silently
# serving the homepage.
#
# /admin is a client-side-routed SPA section (gated by Cloudflare Access,
# never prerendered) — it needs the fallback so any /admin/* sub-path is
# served the same bundle and handled by the router, WITHOUT changing the
# browser's URL (that would break React Router reading the real path).
#
# The rewrite target is dist/admin-shell — deliberately no file extension.
# Confirmed against the real Cloudflare Pages edge: a target ending in
# .html (even a flat, non-nested one) still gets Cloudflare's automatic
# extension-stripping canonicalization applied when served, which turns
# this 200 "rewrite" into a real 308 that changes the visible URL and
# breaks client-side routing. No extension means nothing to strip.
# Content-Type is set explicitly in public/_headers to compensate.
/admin    /admin-shell   200
/admin/*  /admin-shell   200
